hello in this video i explain  how you can test a correlation for  significance  and that's where we start as you know  from my previous video  correlation analysis tests the linear  relationship between variables  in the first step of the correlation  analysis you calculate the correlation  coefficient  for example the pearson correlation  coefficient  or the spearman rank correlation  in general you are interested in whether  there is an association or correlation  in the whole population however  since you cannot survey the entire  population  you use your sample in order to  calculate the correlation  if there is a correlation in a sample  you still have to check  whether this correlation also exists in  the population  therefore we now come to the question of  how we can test the correlation for  significance the significance of  correlation coefficients can be tested  by using a t-test in general  it is tested whether the correlation  coefficient is significantly  different from zero in this case  the null hypothesis is that there is no  linear relationship and the alternative  hypothesis is  that there is a linear relationship we  would now like to test whether the null  hypothesis should be retained  or rejected now you're surely asking the  question  and how can i do that since the  significance of a correlation  coefficient can be tested with a t  test we must of course first calculate  the t  value the t value can be calculated with  this formula  r is the correlation coefficient we  calculated from the sample  and n is the sample size  with t and the sample size we can then  calculate the p value i will show you  how you can easily do this  online in a moment once we have  calculated the p-value  the question arises is the p-value  larger  or smaller than the previously defined  significance level  so we ask is the p-value larger  or smaller if the p-value is greater  the null hypothesis is retained if the  p-value is smaller  the null hypothesis is rejected so the  null hypothesis was there is no  correlation  accordingly if the p-value is greater  than the specified significance level  based on the existing data there is no  correlation in the population  if the p-value is smaller there is a  correlation  in the population and now as promised i  will show you  how you can easily check the correlation  coefficient for significance  online in order to do this  please visit datadeb.net and click  on the online statistics calculator  if you click on clear table you can use  your own data  please make sure the variable names are  in the first row  i will simply use the example data now  afterwards the variables that you copied  into the table above will appear here  below  we want to calculate a correlation so we  click on the  correlation tab let's say we want to  test whether there is a correlation  between  age and salary in order to do this  we simply click on the variable salary  and on the variable h now you can  calculate either the pearson or the  spearman correlation  i simply use the piece now for this  example  below we see the results here we see a  table with the correlations  and the p-value the correlation is  0.679 and the p-value is  0.015  so we can say that the p-value is lower  than the five percent  significance level based on these data  the null hypothesis is rejected  and there is a significant relationship  between  age and income if you like you can also  just have a look at the summary in words  the summary invert says that a pearson  correlation was performed  to test if there is a relationship  between salary and age  the results of the pearson correlation  indicated  that there was a significant positive  association  between salary and age if you want to  know how you can do  many more other analysis with datatab  just watch my next video i look forward  to seeing you  you
 

